.TH PEITOR 1 "2026-09-29" "Peios"
.SH NAME
peitor \- GXWI text editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B peitor
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens a window on the GXWI desktop with a file of text in it, to read and
change. With no
.I file
the window holds a new one, which is asked a name for when it is first saved.
A
.I file
that is not there is made when it is saved.
.PP
One window holds one file. The text belongs to the window and not to the
browser showing it: what has been typed is the same on every device looking
at the session, and is still there when a page is closed and opened again.
Closing the window asks first when there are changes that are not saved.
.PP
Saving writes the file where it is, so that it stays the same file. Saving
under another name makes a new file and never writes over one that is there.
.PP
The file is looked at every two seconds. If something else changes it and
nothing here has changed, it is read again. If both have changed, the editor
asks which is kept.
.PP
Text is UTF-8 with no NUL in it. A file that is anything else is not shown,
and neither is one of more than 349,525 bytes. A file whose lines all end
with a carriage return and a line feed is written back that way.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Save.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+S
Save under another name.
.SH NOTES
Runs within a GXWI session. Its parent supplies the session descriptors and
identity; launch it through the desktop, or open a file with it from a file
explorer.
.SH SEE ALSO
The Peios learn documentation.
